DemoKit's renderer is a derivative work of Cap's AGPLv3 code. It is not
inspired by it; it is a deliberate port, documented as such in the source.
Specifically:

  src/caprender.py
    - `_solve_1d` / `Spring`      <- crates/rendering/src/spring_mass_damper.rs
                                     (analytic under/critical/over-damped solve,
                                     rest thresholds)
    - `zoom_segments`             <- apps/desktop/src-tauri/src/recording.rs
                                     (`generate_zoom_segments_from_clicks_impl`,
                                     including CLICK_PRE_PADDING_MS 300,
                                     CLICK_POST_PADDING_MS 2500, MERGE_GAP_MS 2500,
                                     TRAILING_CLICK_IGNORE_MS 1000,
                                     CLICK_END_CLAMP_PADDING_MS 800, amount 2.0)
    - `build_clusters`,
      `cluster_center_at`,
      `snap_to_edges`,
      `follow_center`,
      `bounds_from`,
      `zoom_timeline`             <- crates/rendering/src/zoom_spring.rs and
                                     crates/rendering/src/zoom.rs
                                     (cluster ratios 0.5/0.7, STEP_MS 8,
                                     CENTER_PREAIM_MAX_AMOUNT, edge snap,
                                     `from_amount_center` travel space)
    - `filter_shake`, `decimate`,
      `pos_at`, `cursor_timeline`,
      `click_t`                   <- crates/rendering/src/cursor_interpolation.rs
                                     (shake filter, 60fps decimation, spring lag
                                     fed forward, click look-ahead 500ms, the
                                     stiffer 175ms pre-click profile, idle hold)
    - cursor sizing, click shrink <- crates/rendering/src/layers/cursor.rs
                                     (STANDARD_CURSOR_HEIGHT 60,
                                      CLICK_SHRINK_SIZE 0.8, 130ms smoothstep,
                                      velocity tilt 0.03 deg/px clamped to 20)
    - shadow, squircle corners    <- crates/rendering/src/shaders/
                                     composite-video-frame.wgsl
                                     (superellipse power 4, smoothstep shadow
                                      falloff over the rounded-rect SDF)

  src/edit.mjs
    - `capZoom`, `buildClusters`  <- the same segment generator and cluster logic

No Cap source file is redistributed here, and no Cap trademark is used. The
cursor images and wallpaper Cap ships are NOT included: DemoKit draws its
cursors as vectors and reads a wallpaper from the host system at run time.

